sequenceDiagram
  participant A as AI model adapter (demo: Muse Wonder / Meta API)
  participant C as Campaign coordinator
  participant W as World runtime
  participant T as Connection adapter (demo: OPC UA)
  participant P as Controller platform (demo: CODESYS Control Win)
  A->>C: World package and initial test plan
  C->>W: Validate and load selected project version
  loop Active execution under current decision policy
    W->>T: Raw input image / service request
    T->>P: Platform-native exchange
    P-->>T: Authentic outputs/status + applied acknowledgement
    T-->>W: Observed response
    W->>W: Evolve physical/device state and next raw signals
    W-->>C: Preserve original observations
  end
  Note over A,P: Model reasoning, transport cadence and controller scan are independent.<br/>Demo OPC UA operating point: 10 Hz; other adapters need separate timing qualification.
  C-->>A: Return evidence from selected experiment
  A->>C: Choose a new hypothesis or follow-up based on evidence
  C->>W: Apply raw-I/O / service intervention
  Note over C,P: Optional HMI actions pass through the coordinator's operator-interface adapter.<br/>A delivered action is distinct from a controller acknowledgement or screen result.
  P-->>T: Actual controller reaction
  T-->>W: Observed response
  W-->>C: Original intervention and outcome evidence
  C-->>A: Expected/observed results and remaining uncertainty
  A->>C: Findings and report
  Note over A,P: Example evidence only: conveyor feedback fault12, recovery,<br/>new D1 contradiction test, fault21, recovery and report.<br/>This example does not define the generic campaign pattern.
